# Keep the build context small and reproducible.
#
# Without this, `docker build` would copy the entire repo — including
# node_modules (hundreds of MB across two frontends), bin/obj, and the local
# .env files that hold real keys. Slower builds, and a real risk of baking a
# secret into an image layer.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/bin
**/obj
**/.git
**/.vs
**/.vscode

# Never ship local configuration or secrets into an image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.*.local.json

# Repo tooling that the API does not need at build time.
ui-shots/
menu/
docs/
.github/
